{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAPy5Z67go2WQCSgmD2Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged` and a test for it. All 10 tests in `sync_watch` pass.\n\n- **`tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`:** `mark_unchanged()` sits next to `mark_changed()`. It sets the receiver's version to the channel's current version, so the current value counts as seen. After that, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send. This is the same as `borrow_and_update()` without borrowing the value.\n- **`tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`:** the new test `rx_mark_unchanged` covers two cases: undoing a `mark_changed()`, and ignoring a value that was really sent.\n\nI didn't run the doc tests or the rest of the test suite, and nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":34465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":266,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"366eefa6-f5e9-43fd-a86e-da9f485706df","uuid":"1102b075-6af8-4b3c-942d-77b365acd04b","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:16:28.094Z","request_id":"req_011CgAPy5NBCwYus4B4fKpiu"}
